       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg per day. That is 5 times the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual 400\u2013800 mg. A dose this high could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg** PO three or four times daily (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day), which is the usual maximum and is typically used for inflammatory conditions\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm the dose with your supervising resident or attending, as you would for any order."
      }
